  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Idaho received $3.8B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. Idaho had 9,806 awards with an average award size of $386K, and obligations are down 4.2% year over year. Idaho’s five-year trend shows fiscal-year obligations of $2.8B in FY21, $2.5B in FY22, $3.2B in FY23, $3.8B in FY24, $3.9B in FY25, and $3.8B in FY26. Idaho’s procurement profile is concentrated: the Department of Energy accounted for $2.7B of obligations, followed by the Department of Agriculture with $610M and the Department of the Interior with $217M. Idaho’s vendor list is dominated by large, single-vendor totals: BATTELLE ENERGY ALLIANCE, LLC received $2.1B and IDAHO ENVIRONMENTAL COALITION LLC received $533M. Idaho’s industry mix reflects heavy spending in professional, scientific, and technical services at $2.1B, remediation services at $539M, and chemical product manufacturing at $342M. All figures are contract obligations; current-year totals are partial (fiscal year to date).",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How did Idaho’s federal contracting change year over year?",
        "body": "Idaho’s obligations are down 4.2% year over year. Idaho received $3.8B in FY2026 to date, which matches the FY24 total of $3.8B and is slightly below FY25’s $3.9B. Idaho’s award count was 9,806 with an average award size of $386K, indicating steady volume with a modest decline in total obligations."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies and vendors drive federal spending in Idaho?",
        "body": "The Department of Energy is the largest buyer in Idaho at $2.7B, followed by the Department of Agriculture at $610M and the Department of the Interior at $217M. BATTELLE ENERGY ALLIANCE, LLC received $2.1B and IDAHO ENVIRONMENTAL COALITION LLC received $533M, reflecting concentrated vendor spending in energy and environmental work."
      }
    ]
